                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Chill little puzzle game. Slow paced, no need to rush, but you will need to think 5 steps ahead in many puzzles.\nSome puzzles can be very short and quick, others can be very long and complex.\nPacing and difficulty progression in Chapter 1 is good- new functions are introduced in a fairly easy puzzle, with the remaining  puzzles getting progressively more challenging. I'll see how the next 2 chapters are, not long from now. But I don't expect them to get easier- not a game for you if you want super-simple-no-brains-needed puzzles. You will have to think. \n\nWASD is all you need (or arrow keys), so this is a game that can be played with one hand only. Coffee in one hand, move the block with the other. I have not tried the game with a controller, so I have no clue whether a controller works well or not.\nThe  colors used are the only major issue I see- this game has no color-blind settings, and some of the puzzles could be next to impossible for people with various forms of color-blindness. There is some slightly annoying music that you can turn down in settings, no audio clues- some sounds when you make a move or use a function/action button in the puzzles- the game is good for Deaf and HoH players, as it can be played with no audio at all without affecting gameplay.\n\nThere are some guides if you get stuck or frustrated, but I find that for me, playing 1 or 2 levels at a time while I am waking up with a cup of coffee is a good way to get my brain set for a day  of work, and if I fail a puzzle and have to start that puzzle over- I don't mind. YMMV. It's good for short sessions if you want a logic puzzle game where you can come and go and take your time to work through the 3 chapters of 50 puzzles each.\n\nNot a game for those who want quick-and-easy achievements- this one will take a little while to earn the 3 achievements. \nGame runs perfectly on a toaster or on a beefy high-end build in Windows or Linux Ubuntu. I have had no bugs or issues on either Windows 10 or Ubuntu 20.04 LTS, no special parameters needed, no compatibility mode needed. The full price is good- not too expensive for what you are getting, but on sale- it's a steal if you enjoy these type of puzzle games.\n\n(quick edit to correct a typo- about halfway through Chapter 2 now- working my way through one puzzle at a time. The puzzles aren't much more difficult, but they are longer- many more steps to reach the end.)",
